#N canvas 20 20 7000 11910 12;
#X text 20 20 display-bench -- the display acceptance run: the display arbiter and the error bus. STEPPED BY HAND: press GO to run the step that has just been described \, press GO again to describe the next one. Nothing moves until you ask it to \, so the PASS IF is on screen and STILL while you read it. The prompt line always says what the next press will do., f 120;
#X text 20 150 GO ON THE MAC: the bng below \, or the dev panel's ENCODER CLICK -- u_mother-stub sends encbut unconditionally and nothing in Cut It consumes it. TURNING the encoder repeats the current step without advancing \, which is what to do when you looked away., f 120;
#X text 2400 200 ⚠️ GO ON THE DEVICE IS NOT THE ENCODER -- IT IS netcat \, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT OPTIONAL. mother only forwards encbut once a patch has asked with /enableEncoder \, and NOTHING IN Cut It EVER ASKS -- m_organelle leaves the encoder out on purpose. So the click that drives this bench on the Mac is silently dead on the Organelle. Send instead with ./test/run.sh --bench <name> from the Mac. ⚠️ NOT netcat: the line this file used to print does nothing on macOS -- BSD nc exits before the datagram is flushed at -w0 \, and -w1 was measured to fail too \, while the port IS bound and the bench is fine. It looks exactly like a dead bench. The device cannot send to itself either: busybox here has no nc at all. Asking mother to enable the encoder is NOT the fix either: that means writing to oscOut \, and g_oled is its sole owner., f 120;
#X text 20 280 Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch -- it only pushes onto the same buses a controller would. A PASS IF is printed for EVERY step including the ones whose correct result is that nothing happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark off., f 120;
#X text 2400 20 ON THE MAC EVERY ERROR STEP ALSO PRINTS /sdcard/cut-it-err.cur: write failed \, AND THAT IS NOT A FAILED STEP. u_err keeps its durable log on the Organelle's SD card \, which no Mac has -- so the write is attempted and refused every time. It is in fact the only proof off-device that the logging path ran at all. On the device that line must NOT appear \, and if it does the card is unwritable and the log is being lost silently., f 120;
#X obj 6000 40 r \$0-say;
#X obj 6000 100 print;
#X text 20 360 GO -- click here \, or the dev panel's encoder button. MAC ONLY -- on the device use netcat \, top right., f 60;
#X obj 20 420 bng 40 250 50 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 20 500 s \$0-go;
#X obj 300 420 r encbut;
#X obj 300 480 select 1;
#X obj 300 540 t b;
#X obj 300 600 s \$0-go;
#X text 560 480 encbut sends 1 THEN 0 \, so select 1 is what stops one press counting twice., f 46;
#X obj 300 680 netreceive 9998 1;
#X obj 300 740 route go;
#X obj 300 800 t b;
#X obj 300 860 s \$0-go;
#X obj 1400 420 r enc;
#X obj 1400 480 t b;
#X obj 1400 540 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 1660 480 enc is 1 for up and 0 for down -- not plus or minus one -- so either direction repeats., f 46;
#X text 20 920 THE STATE MACHINE. phase 0 means the step has been described and not yet run \; phase 1 means it has run. SETTING THE STEP NUMBER IS WHAT DESCRIBES IT \, so advancing is just an increment -- there is no second path to keep in step., f 120;
#X obj 20 980 r \$0-go;
#X obj 20 1040 f;
#X obj 20 1100 select 0 1;
#X obj 300 1040 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1170 t b b;
#X msg 300 1230 1;
#X obj 300 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1290 f;
#X obj 20 1350 s \$0-do-run;
#X obj 900 1170 t b b;
#X msg 1180 1230 0;
#X obj 1180 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 900 1350 f;
#X obj 900 1410 + 1;
#X obj 900 1470 s \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 980 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 1040 t f f f;
#X obj 1700 1110 s \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 1980 1110 s \$0-set-run;
#X obj 1180 1350 r \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 300 1410 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2260 1110 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2100 980 r \$0-repeat;
#X obj 2100 1040 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2500 980 loadbang;
#X obj 2500 1040 del 500;
#X msg 2500 1100 1;
#X obj 2500 1160 s \$0-set-step;
#X text 20 1920 DESCRIBING A STEP. One select per step rather than one wide fan \, so every cord stays short and local -- the same reason u_map chains its routes., f 120;
#X obj 20 2020 r \$0-do-show;
#X obj 20 2080 select 1;
#X obj 240 2080 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2080 === STEP-01-of-14 === Baseline -- nothing is sent;
#X msg 700 2130 PASS IF: Two bars with a small gate mark under each. A BPM at the bottom. Phase 5 hands the footer over from v0.3-ready to the tempo about four seconds in.;
#X msg 700 2180 >>> press GO to run step 1 of 14;
#X obj 240 2250 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2340 select 2;
#X obj 240 2340 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2340 === STEP-02-of-14 === A parameter with a unit -- sending chop-size 43 %;
#X msg 700 2390 PASS IF: chop-size on the top line and a big 43 % under it. The bars shrink to a thin strip. About 1.2 s later the meters come back on their own.;
#X msg 700 2440 >>> press GO to run step 2 of 14;
#X obj 240 2510 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2600 select 3;
#X obj 240 2600 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2600 === STEP-03-of-14 === A parameter with no unit -- sending grain 12;
#X msg 700 2650 PASS IF: grain and then a big 12 with NO PERCENT SIGN left over from the last step. This is the one that matters most.;
#X msg 700 2700 >>> press GO to run step 3 of 14;
#X obj 240 2770 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2860 select 4;
#X obj 240 2860 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2860 === STEP-04-of-14 === A modal -- sending modal recording;
#X msg 700 2910 PASS IF: recording in mid-size text with the bars as a thin strip. Unlike a parameter it STAYS and does not fade.;
#X msg 700 2960 >>> press GO to run step 4 of 14;
#X obj 240 3030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3120 select 5;
#X obj 240 3120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3120 === STEP-05-of-14 === A parameter while a modal is up -- sending chop-size 43 %;
#X msg 700 3170 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES. Still recording. chop-size never appears because the modal outranks it.;
#X msg 700 3220 >>> press GO to run step 5 of 14;
#X obj 240 3290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3380 select 6;
#X obj 240 3380 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3380 === STEP-06-of-14 === A warning over the modal -- sending warn u_root test-warn;
#X msg 700 3430 PASS IF: A bordered box reads warn then u_root then test-warn. About 2 s later it vanishes and RECORDING IS BACK underneath.;
#X msg 700 3480 >>> press GO to run step 6 of 14;
#X obj 240 3550 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3640 select 7;
#X obj 240 3640 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3640 === STEP-07-of-14 === Mode to perform -- nothing is sent to the screen;
#X msg 700 3690 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES. Still recording. Mode is never drawn. This only sets up the next two steps.;
#X msg 700 3740 >>> press GO to run step 7 of 14;
#X obj 240 3810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3900 select 8;
#X obj 240 3900 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3900 === STEP-08-of-14 === A warning while in perform -- sending warn u_root hidden-warn;
#X msg 700 3950 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES. No alert box at all. Still recording. Perform mode suppresses warnings.;
#X msg 700 4000 >>> press GO to run step 8 of 14;
#X obj 240 4070 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4160 select 9;
#X obj 240 4160 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4160 === STEP-09-of-14 === A failure while in perform -- sending fail u_root shown-fail;
#X msg 700 4210 PASS IF: An alert DOES appear reading fail then u_root then shown-fail. Failures are never suppressed. Recording returns after about 4 s.;
#X msg 700 4260 >>> press GO to run step 9 of 14;
#X obj 240 4330 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4420 select 10;
#X obj 240 4420 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4420 === STEP-10-of-14 === Mode back to compose -- nothing is sent to the screen;
#X msg 700 4470 PASS IF: NOTHING CHANGES. Still recording.;
#X msg 700 4520 >>> press GO to run step 10 of 14;
#X obj 240 4590 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4680 select 11;
#X obj 240 4680 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4680 === STEP-11-of-14 === A warning now we are back in compose -- sending warn u_root back-again;
#X msg 700 4730 PASS IF: The alert DOES appear this time reading warn then u_root then back-again. The filter has released.;
#X msg 700 4780 >>> press GO to run step 11 of 14;
#X obj 240 4850 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4940 select 12;
#X obj 240 4940 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4940 === STEP-12-of-14 === Clearing the modal -- sending modal-off;
#X msg 700 4990 PASS IF: recording disappears. You are back to the two meters and the BPM footer.;
#X msg 700 5040 >>> press GO to run step 12 of 14;
#X obj 240 5110 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5200 select 13;
#X obj 240 5200 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5200 === STEP-13-of-14 === The safety timeout -- sending modal stuck and then DELIBERATELY never clearing it;
#X msg 700 5250 PASS IF: stuck appears now. With NO further input it clears itself after 30 s. The next step is 35 s away.;
#X msg 700 5300 >>> press GO to run step 13 of 14;
#X obj 240 5370 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5460 select 14;
#X obj 240 5460 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5460 === STEP-14-of-14 === The 30 second safety timeout -- the deferred half of step 13;
#X msg 700 5510 PASS IF: The screen returned to the meters on its own during that 35 s wait. That was the safety timeout.;
#X msg 700 5560 >>> press GO to run step 14 of 14;
#X obj 240 5630 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5720 t b;
#X msg 240 5720 === BENCH COMPLETE === every step has been run -- reload the patch to go round again;
#X obj 240 5780 s \$0-say;
#X text 20 5860 RUNNING A STEP. The actions fire in the order they are listed -- rightmost trigger outlet first -- and the line saying the step has fired goes out LAST \, off outlet 0 \, so it cannot arrive before the thing it describes., f 120;
#X obj 20 5960 r \$0-do-run;
#X obj 20 6020 select 1;
#X obj 240 6020 t b;
